  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">My new volume of videos—the 56th, if you can believe it!—is out now. In it, I discuss leaky gut, inflammation, the potato series I presented in a webinar a few months ago, and more. It is </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">available</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> as a streaming video so you can start watching it immediately. Each video in this new collection will be released online over the next few months, available for free, of course, but if you don’t want to wait, you can watch all of them by streaming </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/downloads\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">right now</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">And, remember, if you watch the videos on </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> or </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/NutritionFactsOrg\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">YouTube</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, you can access captions in several different languages. To find yours, click on the settings wheel in the lower-right of the video and then “Subtitles/CC.” Happy viewing!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you are a $25+ monthly supporter and opted in to our</span> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/rewards/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">donor rewards</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, you’re likely already an expert on these new topics by now, since you already received a complimentary link to the new download. If you’d like early access to new videos before they’re available to the public, please consider becoming a </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/?mc_cid=1b9efb2a80&amp;mc_eid=[UNIQID]/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">monthly supporter</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Without your generosity, we wouldn’t be able to continue our work.</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Thank you!</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Roasted Kabocha with Kale-Cranberry Stuffing</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182.jpg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-70446  alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-1024x1025.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-1024x1025.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-960x961.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-768x769.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-1200x1201.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-720x721.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182-540x541.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Roasted-Kabocha-with-Kale-Cranberry-Stuffing_-e1637082852182.jpg 1995w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Kabocha is a Japanese pumpkin, and this recipe makes a perfect, hearty meal. Rather than bread cubes, the stuffing for this dish is made with my Basic BROL, combined with onion, celery, kale, and cranberries. The recipe, originally published in </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The How Not to Diet Cookbook</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, can be </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/roasted-kabocha-with-kale-cranberry-stuffing/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">found here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. And see our Instagram for </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CLpZjzgAHpp/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">a video</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on how it’s made.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Sweet Potatoes</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog.jpg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-70442 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/KT-sweet-potatoes-blog.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>During the </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">harsh Boston winters while I was in medical school, I would take two freshly microwaved sweet potatoes and pop them into my coat pockets to keep my hands warm. After they cooled down, I had healthy snacks on the go! They are one of my favorite vegetables, and I regularly eat them to check off the “other vegetables” boxes on my Daily Dozen checklist</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For more information and </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">my videos on this subject, visit the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/sweet-potatoes/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>New Plant-Based Nut</b><b>rition Degree</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I’m frequently asked, “How can I promote evidence-based nutrition professionally?” There’s a new way to get involved in our field! Loma Linda University has just launched a new Master of Science in Plant-Based Nutrition program. Check out the details </span><a href=\"http://llucatalog.llu.edu/public-health/nutrition/ms/#text\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Volunteer Spotlight: Joan Davis</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-70440 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-1024x1528.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"297\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-1024x1528.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-960x1432.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-768x1146.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-1200x1791.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-720x1074.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan-540x806.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/joan.jpg 1530w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 199px) 100vw, 199px\"/></a>“During the last five years, I have moderated questions and responses from commenters on the videos and blogs Dr. Greger so brilliantly creates. As a nurse and former teacher, I appreciate the opportunity to provide responses that often involve some clarification, detective work, and sometimes even new discoveries. The chance to do this every week makes it especially rewarding to contribute to NF’s important, life-saving goals!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">My favorite whole food, plant-based meal is a green salad loaded with beans and healthy carbs, and topped with seeds, nuts, and sprouts!”</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Flash Sale Going on Now</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-70438 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/11/Black-Friday-Sale-v2-1080-Mailchimp.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Our extended Black Friday sale is live and will run through November 29! All merch on </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DrGreger.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is 20% off, including a couple of brand-new, limited-time items. <a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/merch\">Check it out</a>.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Top Three Videos</b></h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68406 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Hand raised showing a rock sign over the crowd at heavy metal concert\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-14-The-Dangerous-Effects-of-Heavy-Metal-Music.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-dangerous-effects-of-heavy-metal-music/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Dangerous Effects of Heavy Metal Music</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: How might we moderate the rare but very real risk of headbanging?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68396 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Wooden bowl with raw mushrooms on a dark background\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-12-Medicinal-Mushrooms-for-Cancer-Survival.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/medicinal-mushrooms-for-cancer-survival/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Medicinal Mushrooms for Cancer Survival</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: Did the five randomized controlled trials of reishi mushrooms in cancer patients show benefits in terms of tumor response rate, survival time, or quality of life?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68411 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Multigrain cereals with fresh berry\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-15-Ochratoxin-in-Breakfast-Cereals.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/ochratoxin-in-breakfast-cereals/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ochratoxin in Breakfast Cereals</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: One of the few food contaminants found at higher levels in those eating plant-based diets are mycotoxins, fungal toxins in moldy food ingredients, such as oats.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Live Q&amp;As</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-68737 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"image of dr greger\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Due to my writing schedule for my next book, </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Age</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, I will be taking a break from Q&amp;As until April 2022. In the meantime, you can find links to past live Q&amp;As </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on NutritionFacts.org. And, remember, I have an </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">audio podcast</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to keep you company, too. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
